{
  "nodes": [
    {
      "id": "C1",
      "type": "text",
      "text": "**C1** [claim]\nOptimal incentive targeting is characterized by decomposing interventions into network principal components.",
      "x": 0,
      "y": 690,
      "width": 270,
      "height": 120
    },
    {
      "id": "N1",
      "type": "text",
      "text": "**N1** [result]\nCorollary 1: similarity ratios are ordered decreasing under complements and increasing under substitutes.",
      "x": 360,
      "y": 690,
      "width": 270,
      "height": 120,
      "color": "1"
    },
    {
      "id": "prop_3",
      "type": "text",
      "text": "**prop_3** [proposition]\nProposition 3: mean-shift uncertainty reduces to the deterministic problem at the expected status quo vector.",
      "x": 720,
      "y": 690,
      "width": 270,
      "height": 120,
      "color": "1"
    },
    {
      "id": "C2",
      "type": "text",
      "text": "**C2** [claim]\nStrategic complements emphasize top principal components, while strategic substitutes emphasize bottom principal components.",
      "x": 0,
      "y": 460,
      "width": 270,
      "height": 120
    },
    {
      "id": "C5",
      "type": "text",
      "text": "**C5** [claim]\nUnder incomplete information, the same principal-component ordering extends through mean shifts and variance control.",
      "x": 360,
      "y": 460,
      "width": 270,
      "height": 120
    },
    {
      "id": "prop_1",
      "type": "text",
      "text": "**prop_1** [proposition]\nProposition 1: small-budget ratios converge to alpha ratios; large-budget interventions converge to first or last principal component.",
      "x": 720,
      "y": 460,
      "width": 270,
      "height": 120,
      "color": "1"
    },
    {
      "id": "C3",
      "type": "text",
      "text": "**C3** [claim]\nFor large budgets, optimal interventions become simple and align with a single principal component.",
      "x": 0,
      "y": 230,
      "width": 270,
      "height": 120
    },
    {
      "id": "prop_2",
      "type": "text",
      "text": "**prop_2** [proposition]\nProposition 2: sufficient budget bounds make simple interventions nearly welfare-optimal and close in cosine similarity.",
      "x": 360,
      "y": 230,
      "width": 270,
      "height": 120,
      "color": "1"
    },
    {
      "id": "prop_oa1",
      "type": "text",
      "text": "**prop_oa1** [proposition]\nProposition OA1: for general small-budget costs satisfying OA2, similarity ratios converge to alpha ratios.",
      "x": 720,
      "y": 230,
      "width": 270,
      "height": 120,
      "color": "1"
    },
    {
      "id": "C4",
      "type": "text",
      "text": "**C4** [claim]\nThe budget threshold for simple near-optimal interventions is governed by the top or bottom spectral gap.",
      "x": 0,
      "y": 0,
      "width": 270,
      "height": 120
    },
    {
      "id": "C6",
      "type": "text",
      "text": "**C6** [claim]\nThe principal-component logic extends beyond the baseline model to broader costs, externalities, nonsymmetric matrices, and linear-cost cases.",
      "x": 360,
      "y": 0,
      "width": 270,
      "height": 120
    },
    {
      "id": "N8",
      "type": "text",
      "text": "**N8** [definition]\nSimilarity ratio divides optimal-intervention similarity by status-quo similarity for a component.",
      "x": 0,
      "y": 920,
      "width": 270,
      "height": 120
    },
    {
      "id": "thm_1",
      "type": "text",
      "text": "**thm_1** [proposition]\nTheorem 1: optimal intervention similarities are proportional to status quo similarity and an eigenvalue-budget multiplier.",
      "x": 360,
      "y": 920,
      "width": 270,
      "height": 120,
      "color": "1"
    },
    {
      "id": "eq_6",
      "type": "text",
      "text": "**eq_6** [equation]\nBudget equation pinning down the Lagrange multiplier mu.",
      "x": 0,
      "y": 1610,
      "width": 270,
      "height": 120
    },
    {
      "id": "prop_4",
      "type": "text",
      "text": "**prop_4** [proposition]\nProposition 4: variance-control interventions rank variance allocation across principal components by alpha and by the sign of w.",
      "x": 360,
      "y": 1610,
      "width": 270,
      "height": 120,
      "color": "1"
    },
    {
      "id": "N24",
      "type": "text",
      "text": "**N24** [result]\nFor nonsymmetric G, the relevant decomposition becomes singular vectors rather than G's eigenvectors.",
      "x": 0,
      "y": 2530,
      "width": 270,
      "height": 120
    },
    {
      "id": "PA",
      "type": "text",
      "text": "**PA** [assumption]\nProperty A: aggregate equilibrium utility is proportional to squared equilibrium actions.",
      "x": 360,
      "y": 2530,
      "width": 270,
      "height": 120,
      "color": "1"
    },
    {
      "id": "eq_3",
      "type": "text",
      "text": "**eq_3** [equation]\nClosed-form equilibrium a* = [I - beta G]^{-1}b.",
      "x": 720,
      "y": 2530,
      "width": 270,
      "height": 120
    },
    {
      "id": "prop_oa2",
      "type": "text",
      "text": "**prop_oa2** [proposition]\nProposition OA2: OA2 plus homogeneity makes intervention costs orthogonally invariant.",
      "x": 1080,
      "y": 2530,
      "width": 270,
      "height": 120
    },
    {
      "id": "eq_7",
      "type": "text",
      "text": "**eq_7** [equation]\nNetwork multiplier alpha_ell = (1 - beta lambda_ell)^{-2}.",
      "x": 0,
      "y": 2070,
      "width": 270,
      "height": 120,
      "color": "4"
    },
    {
      "id": "eq_8",
      "type": "text",
      "text": "**eq_8** [equation]\nExpected welfare under incomplete information decomposes by principal-component means and variances.",
      "x": 360,
      "y": 2070,
      "width": 270,
      "height": 120
    },
    {
      "id": "prop_oa3",
      "type": "text",
      "text": "**prop_oa3** [proposition]\nProposition OA3: under linear intervention costs, the optimum targets a single individual.",
      "x": 720,
      "y": 2070,
      "width": 270,
      "height": 120
    },
    {
      "id": "A1",
      "type": "text",
      "text": "**A1** [assumption]\nThe adjacency matrix G is symmetric.",
      "x": 0,
      "y": 2990,
      "width": 270,
      "height": 120,
      "color": "4"
    },
    {
      "id": "A2",
      "type": "text",
      "text": "**A2** [assumption]\nThe spectral radius of beta G is less than 1 and G has distinct eigenvalues.",
      "x": 360,
      "y": 2990,
      "width": 270,
      "height": 120,
      "color": "4"
    },
    {
      "id": "A3",
      "type": "text",
      "text": "**A3** [assumption]\nThe planner's bliss point is not already reachable: either w<0 with insufficient budget or w>0.",
      "x": 720,
      "y": 2990,
      "width": 270,
      "height": 120,
      "color": "4"
    },
    {
      "id": "A4",
      "type": "text",
      "text": "**A4** [assumption]\nMean-shift interventions have squared Euclidean cost and other random interventions are infeasible.",
      "x": 1080,
      "y": 2990,
      "width": 270,
      "height": 120,
      "color": "4"
    },
    {
      "id": "A5",
      "type": "text",
      "text": "**A5** [assumption]\nVariance-control costs are mean-neutral and invariant to orthogonal rotations around the mean.",
      "x": 1440,
      "y": 2990,
      "width": 270,
      "height": 120,
      "color": "4"
    },
    {
      "id": "N10",
      "type": "text",
      "text": "**N10** [mechanism]\nStrategic spillovers can be complements or substitutes, changing whether neighbors' incentives move together or against each other.",
      "x": 1800,
      "y": 2990,
      "width": 270,
      "height": 120,
      "color": "4"
    },
    {
      "id": "N17",
      "type": "text",
      "text": "**N17** [definition]\nIncomplete-information intervention chooses a random vector B over standalone marginal returns.",
      "x": 2160,
      "y": 2990,
      "width": 270,
      "height": 120,
      "color": "4"
    },
    {
      "id": "N2",
      "type": "text",
      "text": "**N2** [definition]\nBaseline game: simultaneous-move continuous-action network game.",
      "x": 2520,
      "y": 2990,
      "width": 270,
      "height": 120,
      "color": "4"
    },
    {
      "id": "N3",
      "type": "text",
      "text": "**N3** [definition]\nStandalone marginal return b_i is the part of marginal return independent of others' actions.",
      "x": 2880,
      "y": 2990,
      "width": 270,
      "height": 120,
      "color": "4"
    },
    {
      "id": "N4",
      "type": "text",
      "text": "**N4** [definition]\nIntervention changes the status quo vector of standalone marginal returns subject to a budget.",
      "x": 3240,
      "y": 2990,
      "width": 270,
      "height": 120,
      "color": "4"
    },
    {
      "id": "N5",
      "type": "text",
      "text": "**N5** [definition]\nPrincipal components are the eigenvectors that diagonalize the symmetric interaction matrix G.",
      "x": 3600,
      "y": 2990,
      "width": 270,
      "height": 120,
      "color": "4"
    },
    {
      "id": "N6",
      "type": "text",
      "text": "**N6** [definition]\nProjection onto a principal component gives a vector's magnitude in that component.",
      "x": 3960,
      "y": 2990,
      "width": 270,
      "height": 120,
      "color": "4"
    },
    {
      "id": "N7",
      "type": "text",
      "text": "**N7** [definition]\nCosine similarity measures how aligned two nonzero vectors are.",
      "x": 4320,
      "y": 2990,
      "width": 270,
      "height": 120,
      "color": "4"
    },
    {
      "id": "OA1",
      "type": "text",
      "text": "**OA1** [assumption]\nOnline Appendix OA1: total interaction is constant across individuals.",
      "x": 4680,
      "y": 2990,
      "width": 270,
      "height": 120,
      "color": "4"
    },
    {
      "id": "OA2",
      "type": "text",
      "text": "**OA2** [assumption]\nOnline Appendix OA2: general costs are translation-invariant, symmetric, nonnegative, locally separable, and smooth at zero.",
      "x": 5040,
      "y": 2990,
      "width": 270,
      "height": 120,
      "color": "4"
    },
    {
      "id": "OA3",
      "type": "text",
      "text": "**OA3** [assumption]\nOnline Appendix OA3: intervention costs are homogeneous under scaling.",
      "x": 5400,
      "y": 2990,
      "width": 270,
      "height": 120,
      "color": "4"
    },
    {
      "id": "eq_1",
      "type": "text",
      "text": "**eq_1** [equation]\nPayoff equation for individual utility in the linear-quadratic network game.",
      "x": 5760,
      "y": 2990,
      "width": 270,
      "height": 120,
      "color": "4"
    },
    {
      "id": "N11",
      "type": "text",
      "text": "**N11** [mechanism]\nOrthogonal principal components separate intervention effects so each component can be evaluated independently.",
      "x": 0,
      "y": 2760,
      "width": 270,
      "height": 120,
      "color": "4"
    },
    {
      "id": "N12",
      "type": "text",
      "text": "**N12** [mechanism]\nStatus quo similarity determines how much an initial incentive profile loads on each component.",
      "x": 360,
      "y": 2760,
      "width": 270,
      "height": 120
    },
    {
      "id": "N18",
      "type": "text",
      "text": "**N18** [mechanism]\nExpected welfare depends only on first and second moments of principal-component projections.",
      "x": 720,
      "y": 2760,
      "width": 270,
      "height": 120
    },
    {
      "id": "N19",
      "type": "text",
      "text": "**N19** [definition]\nMean-shift intervention adds a deterministic vector y to the random status quo.",
      "x": 1080,
      "y": 2760,
      "width": 270,
      "height": 120,
      "color": "4"
    },
    {
      "id": "N20",
      "type": "text",
      "text": "**N20** [mechanism]\nVariance-control cost neutrality makes the benefits side determine which components receive variance.",
      "x": 1440,
      "y": 2760,
      "width": 270,
      "height": 120,
      "color": "4"
    },
    {
      "id": "N21",
      "type": "text",
      "text": "**N21** [data]\nInvestment-game example satisfies the baseline structure and Property A with welfare proportional to squared actions.",
      "x": 1800,
      "y": 2760,
      "width": 270,
      "height": 120
    },
    {
      "id": "N22",
      "type": "text",
      "text": "**N22** [data]\nLocal-public-good example satisfies the structure with strategic substitutes and positive externalities.",
      "x": 2160,
      "y": 2760,
      "width": 270,
      "height": 120
    },
    {
      "id": "N23",
      "type": "text",
      "text": "**N23** [definition]\nLinear-cost intervention problem uses an L1 budget on changes to standalone marginal returns.",
      "x": 2520,
      "y": 2760,
      "width": 270,
      "height": 120,
      "color": "4"
    },
    {
      "id": "N9",
      "type": "text",
      "text": "**N9** [definition]\nSimple interventions allocate the whole budget along the first component under complements or the last under substitutes.",
      "x": 2880,
      "y": 2760,
      "width": 270,
      "height": 120
    },
    {
      "id": "eq_2",
      "type": "text",
      "text": "**eq_2** [equation]\nNash equilibrium linear system [I - beta G]a* = b.",
      "x": 3240,
      "y": 2760,
      "width": 270,
      "height": 120
    },
    {
      "id": "eq_9",
      "type": "text",
      "text": "**eq_9** [equation]\nExample variance-control cost depends on the total variance when the mean is fixed.",
      "x": 3600,
      "y": 2760,
      "width": 270,
      "height": 120,
      "color": "4"
    },
    {
      "id": "eq_4",
      "type": "text",
      "text": "**eq_4** [equation]\nPrincipal-component equilibrium response a*_ell = b_ell/(1-beta lambda_ell).",
      "x": 0,
      "y": 2300,
      "width": 270,
      "height": 120
    },
    {
      "id": "eq_IT",
      "type": "text",
      "text": "**eq_IT** [equation]\nIncentive-targeting problem: choose b to maximize equilibrium welfare subject to equilibrium and budget constraints.",
      "x": 360,
      "y": 2300,
      "width": 270,
      "height": 120,
      "color": "4"
    },
    {
      "id": "N16",
      "type": "text",
      "text": "**N16** [mechanism]\nSmall spectral or bottom gaps make different principal components similarly amplified, delaying simplicity.",
      "x": 0,
      "y": 1150,
      "width": 270,
      "height": 120
    },
    {
      "id": "eq_5",
      "type": "text",
      "text": "**eq_5** [equation]\nTheorem 1 similarity proportionality for the optimal intervention.",
      "x": 360,
      "y": 1150,
      "width": 270,
      "height": 120
    },
    {
      "id": "N13",
      "type": "text",
      "text": "**N13** [mechanism]\nThe eigenvalue and budget determine a component's network multiplier in the optimal intervention.",
      "x": 0,
      "y": 1380,
      "width": 270,
      "height": 120
    },
    {
      "id": "N14",
      "type": "text",
      "text": "**N14** [mechanism]\nOrdering of alpha coefficients maps to eigenvalue ordering differently for complements and substitutes.",
      "x": 0,
      "y": 1840,
      "width": 270,
      "height": 120
    },
    {
      "id": "N15",
      "type": "text",
      "text": "**N15** [mechanism]\nThe Lagrange multiplier equalizes marginal return and marginal cost across active principal components.",
      "x": 360,
      "y": 1840,
      "width": 270,
      "height": 120
    },
    {
      "id": "finding_F003",
      "type": "text",
      "text": "**F003**  (material/proof)\nTheorem 1 omits a genericity hypothesis used in its proof's change of variables",
      "x": 6460,
      "y": 0,
      "width": 330,
      "height": 120,
      "color": "2"
    },
    {
      "id": "finding_F001",
      "type": "text",
      "text": "**F001**  (material/framing)\nAbstract's 'simplicity' claim overstates what Proposition 1 establishes",
      "x": 6460,
      "y": 170,
      "width": 330,
      "height": 120,
      "color": "2"
    },
    {
      "id": "finding_F004",
      "type": "text",
      "text": "**F004**  (material/robustness)\nProp 2's near-optimal simple-intervention result hinges on a budget threshold",
      "x": 6460,
      "y": 340,
      "width": 330,
      "height": 120,
      "color": "2"
    },
    {
      "id": "finding_F010",
      "type": "text",
      "text": "**F010**  (material/framing)\nProp 4 variance-ordering depends on the directional neutrality of Assumption 5",
      "x": 6460,
      "y": 510,
      "width": 330,
      "height": 120,
      "color": "2"
    },
    {
      "id": "finding_F012",
      "type": "text",
      "text": "**F012**  (material/notation)\nOA3.1 reparameterization denominator should be the status-quo component",
      "x": 6460,
      "y": 680,
      "width": 330,
      "height": 120,
      "color": "2"
    },
    {
      "id": "finding_F008",
      "type": "text",
      "text": "**F008**  (material/notation)\nLemma OA1 Perron eigenvector entries: sqrt(n) should be 1/sqrt(n)",
      "x": 6460,
      "y": 850,
      "width": 330,
      "height": 120,
      "color": "2"
    },
    {
      "id": "finding_F005",
      "type": "text",
      "text": "**F005**  (material/robustness)\nMethodological-contribution framing (principal-components decomposition)",
      "x": 6460,
      "y": 1020,
      "width": 330,
      "height": 120,
      "color": "2"
    }
  ],
